# Raw Markdown for Written Output

When the user wants **written output** in the CLI (CHANGELOG summaries, release notes, docs drafts, copy-pasteable text, etc.) -- anything meant to be read or copied as markdown source -- show the **actual markdown characters**, not a rendered version.

## Why

Rendered replies hide `#` / `###` and turn `-` lists into bullet symbols (`•`). The user cannot verify or copy the source as intended.

## Do

- Put that content in a fenced code block (e.g. ` ```markdown ` ... ` ``` `) so `#`, `-`, and other markup stay as plain text.
- Apply this to final deliverable prose, not to agent build plans, tool traces, or normal conversational replies.

## Don't

- Rely on the chat UI's markdown rendering for copy-pasteable written deliverables.
- Use Unicode bullet characters (`•`, `●`, etc.) in place of markdown list markers.

```markdown
<!-- ❌ BAD: rendered in the reply as bullets / headings -->
### New
- Item one

<!-- ✅ GOOD: fenced so source is visible -->
### New
- Item one
```

(The good example must live inside a fenced code block in the real reply.)
